# What must never reach the image (week 1 task 5).
#
# Two kinds of entry: the heavy (a 5 GB venv, a Next build, the git history)
# and the private (keys, databases, logs). The build context is sent to the
# daemon in full before anything runs, so a missing line here costs both size
# and secrecy.

# Heavy — and wrong: a venv built on the host is the host's interpreter.
venv
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.github

# Private — keys never enter an image. .env.template is the shipped example and
# is the one file of the family that does.
.env*
!.env.template

# Her memory and your identity are mounted at runtime, never baked in.
#
# `COPY . /app` takes the whole context, so an exclusion of only the databases
# still shipped data/delegations/ (host credentials), data/agent_sessions/,
# data/arbiter/, data/present_moment/ and the owner/user identity files into a
# layer anyone with the image can read. Everything under data/ is out; the one
# exception is the shipped example the first preflight seeds the config from.
data/**
!data/palli.example.yaml
identity/owners
identity/users
identity/palli
backups
logs

# The dashboard's build inputs and outputs — rebuilt in the image if needed.
website/node_modules
website/.next

# Working files that are not the product.
.superpowers
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
